cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this doctrine, please cite it as below. The French corpus is authoritative."
title: "MYSTANCE: the human layer of AI systems"
authors:
  - family-names: "Noto"
    given-names: "Julien-Pierre"
    alias: "JP Noto"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  MYSTANCE is a doctrine for the human-AI relationship: a tuned relationship
  with one cardinal parameter, the assistance level, set on four named
  behavioral-contract levels on a closed scale (mediation to framed
  generation: never zero mediation, never 100% AI production); a second
  orthogonal parameter, the stance (how the assistant carries itself, from a
  closed list); a canonical scaffolding pattern ("3 proposals + free
  choice"); locked templates (structure owned by the doctrine, content owned
  by the user); and user-owned, deferrable assistant naming. The level
  modulates how much the AI proposes, never who decides.
keywords:
  - human-AI interaction
  - assistance level
  - AI adoption
  - user sovereignty
  - locked templates
repository-code: "https://github.com/JP-Noto/MYSTANCE"
